# ---------------------------------------------------------------- deal data
# This repository is PUBLIC. Everything below is either a real person's data or
# our own outreach infrastructure, and neither belongs in it. The CODE is the
# shareable part; what it produces is not.
#
# Deal deliverables and research packs name real owners and heirs, carry their
# addresses, phone numbers and in the probate work their dates of death. A
# public commit of that is not undoable: forks, caches and archives keep it
# after any later deletion.
*.xlsx
*_Deep_Prospecting.md
*_Deep_Prospecting.pdf
*_Outreach.csv
*contacts*.csv
walk_*.json
*_boundary.json

# Property photos and video from walkthroughs (141MB, and they show real homes).
158 Old State/
*.MOV
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png

# Our sending numbers and the internal uuid -> caller name map. Publishing the
# number pool invites exactly the abuse the pool exists to avoid, and these
# live on the Fly volume at /data in production anyway.
config/sms_numbers.json
config/sms_senders.json

# Superseded deal-workbook versions, moved out of the repo root by the
# cleanup pass. Kept on disk with a MANIFEST.csv so any of it can be put
# back, but it is derived output and does not belong in git.
#
# archive/notice_screenshots/ is the exception and is tracked: it is retired
# SOURCE, not derived output, and CLAUDE.md sends readers to it by name. Same
# `dir/*` + `!` form as deals/ above, for the same parent-directory reason.
archive/*
!archive/notice_screenshots/

# Per-deal spec files for the lender package and the post-walkthrough pack.
# The lender/borrower fields are placeholder-scrubbed but the rest is not:
# real contract prices, real seller names, real comps on real addresses.
# The GENERATOR is the shareable part; a filled-in spec is deal data.
# deals/EXAMPLE_lender_spec.json is the scrubbed starting point and is kept.
# Note the `deals/*` form. Git cannot re-include a file with `!` once its
# PARENT DIRECTORY is excluded, so `deals/` + `!deals/EXAMPLE...` silently
# drops the example. Excluding the contents instead keeps the negation live.
deals/*
!deals/EXAMPLE_lender_spec.json

# Skip-trace and list exports. Real owners, real phone numbers.
vacant_top100*.csv
*_top100*.csv
